, 5, 7, 11, 13]","primes.lowerBound(6)      \/\/ 3, the index of 7"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A sorted set kept in an AVL tree: a binary search tree in which the heights of every vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two subtrees differ by at most one (Adelson-Velsky and Landis, 1962).","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/init()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/init(_:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/height"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/elements(in:)-27opt","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/elements(in:)-7qo69","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/lowerBound(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/max()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree\/min()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLT